    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0189" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/2–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Malta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-01">February 1,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cricket<anchor n="46" xml:id="d144-f1"/> 45. Have dispatched the following to
                    Winant after conference which Eden and I had with General Marshall<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d144-f2"/> and Field Marshal Sir Alan Brooke.<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d144-f3"/>
                </p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“You are authorized immediately to inform the European Advisory Commission of
                        this Government’s approval of the protocol on zones of occupation for
                        Germany. Eden is likewise telegraphing the British Government’s
                        approval.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Please advise McCloy.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="46" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
                <p>Series designation for telegrams from the Malta Conference. For record of the
                    conference at Malta, January 30–February 2, 1945, between President Roosevelt
                    and British Prime Minister Churchill, with their advisers, see <ref
                        target="frus1945Malta#pg_459">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Conferences at Malta and Yalta</hi>, 1945, pp.
                        459</ref>–<ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_546">546</ref>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f2" n="47" xml:id="d144-f2-content">
                <p>General of the Army George C. Marshall, Chief of Staff, U.S. Army</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f3" n="48" xml:id="d144-f3-content">
                <p>Chief of the British Imperial General Staff</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
